WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:01.500
- What we're going to do in this video

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:06.400
is look at two rectangles
that have the exact same area,

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:08.130
and we're going to measure each of them

00:00:08.130 --> 00:00:10.690
with a different square unit.

00:00:10.690 --> 00:00:14.230
So this top unit right over
here, this is a square foot.

00:00:14.230 --> 00:00:18.610
So that means its height is one foot

00:00:18.610 --> 00:00:22.903
and it's width right here is one foot.

00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:25.900
Now, this is square unit over here,

00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:28.220
this is completely made up.

00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:32.010
And I'm going to call
this a voot or a voot.

00:00:32.010 --> 00:00:37.010
So, this right over here is one voot

00:00:37.870 --> 00:00:41.480
and this over here,
the width, is one voot.

00:00:42.860 --> 00:00:47.050
So this entire thing is a one square voot,

00:00:49.840 --> 00:00:54.610
while this top one, of
course, is one square voot.

00:00:56.820 --> 00:01:00.135
Now, let's measure the top rectangle

00:01:00.135 --> 00:01:01.594
in terms of square feet,

00:01:01.594 --> 00:01:02.843
and let's measure the bottom
rectangle in terms of square,

00:01:04.401 --> 00:01:07.179
I guess I could say veet,
(chuckles) all right.

00:01:07.179 --> 00:01:09.429
So first the top rectangle.

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:15.560
So we have one, two square feet,

00:01:15.960 --> 00:01:18.840
three square feet,

00:01:18.840 --> 00:01:23.840
four square feet, five square feet,

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:28.890
and then we have, looks
like six square feet.

00:01:30.380 --> 00:01:32.800
And then we're gonna need to
have another six square feet

00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:34.090
down here.

00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:39.090
So that's seven, eight,
nine, 10, 11, and 12.

00:01:45.690 --> 00:01:47.370
So when I tile these square feet

00:01:47.370 --> 00:01:48.720
onto our original rectangle,

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:50.900
it looks like we have 12 square feet.

00:01:50.900 --> 00:01:55.740
And so I could write it's area
like this, 12 square feet.

00:01:58.180 --> 00:02:00.883
Now what about this one in terms of veet?

00:02:01.730 --> 00:02:04.500
You could have a square
voot or many square veet.

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:07.470
Let me do the same exercise here.

00:02:07.470 --> 00:02:09.510
That's one square voot,

00:02:10.510 --> 00:02:15.510
this is two square veet, I could say,

00:02:15.520 --> 00:02:19.790
and then this is three square veet.

00:02:19.790 --> 00:02:23.850
So the same area could
either be 12 square feet

00:02:23.850 --> 00:02:28.140
or it could be three square veet.

00:02:31.010 --> 00:02:33.470
And I want you to think about
whether that makes sense.

00:02:33.470 --> 00:02:35.210
Think about how many square feet

00:02:35.210 --> 00:02:37.230
would make up one square voot.

00:02:37.230 --> 00:02:40.810
In fact, we can figure that
out on our own right over here.

00:02:40.810 --> 00:02:45.810
So that's one square foot,
this is two square feet,

00:02:45.920 --> 00:02:50.920
this is three square feet,
and then four square feet.

00:02:51.460 --> 00:02:56.020
So it looks like four square
feet make up one square voot.

00:02:56.020 --> 00:02:56.853
And so think about,

00:02:56.853 --> 00:02:59.760
does it make sense that three square veet

00:02:59.760 --> 00:03:03.093
is the same thing as 12 square feet?

